VulkanOptics (optics::)
======================

Reusable deterministic BVH material compositor for mirrors and glass.
The host owns rasterization, G-buffers, VulkanWrapper, swapchain and command
buffers. Optics builds and owns its CPU SAH stackless BVH and GPU face/node/
index buffers using the shared VulkanBVH builder. No photon transport,
photon buffers, alternative GI renderer or hardware RT extension is required.

The host provides triangles, per-face UVs, normal/PBR data and source textures.
A bounded ray path traces mirror/glass interactions and shades off-screen hits
with PCloud's existing 3D GI probes and direct lights. Default mirrors require
no stochastic denoising. Thin glass has straight-through transmission, tint
and Fresnel reflection. Material atlases preserve UV, alpha cutout, normal,
metallic/roughness, AO and emissive inputs.

Light changes preserve BVH topology; animated triangles refit it using
per-swapchain frame buffers. Scissor regions avoid fullscreen traversal.
Planar mirrors can reuse rasterized reflected-camera lighting.

Limitations: large optical coverage and CPU skinning/refit need profiling;
off-screen PBR channel parity and M2 GPU performance need native validation.
Texture atlases are bounded at 8192x8192.

Public API: optics/optics.hpp; shaders: optics/shaders/.
